        "event": "Flood Warning",
        "headline": "Flood Warning issued October 2 at 6:50AM AKDT until October 3 at 7:45AM AKDT by NWS Juneau AK",
        "description": "The Mendenhall Lake crested early Friday morning, and the Mendenhall\nRiver will crest shortly. Flooding is ongoing, and is expected to\ncontinue near Mendenhall Lake and River before coming to an end later\nthis morning as water levels decrease rapidly behind the crest.\n\n* WHAT...Flooding caused by a glacier-dammed lake outburst continues.\n\n* WHERE...The Mendenhall Lake And River near the Mendenhall Glacier\nRecreation area, View Drive and below Back Loop bridge.\n\n* WHEN...Until 745 AM AKDT Saturda",
        "severity": "Severe",
        "certainty": "Likely",
        "urgency": "Immediate",
        "sender": "NWS Juneau AK",
        "effective": "2026-10-02T06:50:00-08:00",
        "expires": "2026-10-02T15:00:00-08:00",
        "areas": "City and Borough of Juneau",
        "category": "Met",
        "response": "Avoid",
        "instruction": "Stay tuned to further developments by listening to your local radio,\ntelevision, or NOAA Weather Radio for further information.\n\nTurn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.\n\nBe especially cautious at night when it is harder to recognize the\ndangers ",
        "lat": 58.408181818181816,
        "lng": -134.56272727272727
      },
